# The second site, whose default store is Azure Cosmos DB, under its own name
# (ADR: A permanent address for the second site). These sit above everything in
# netlify.toml, because Netlify reads this file's rules first and the first
# matching rule wins.
#
# Every page is the bare path with a query naming the view, the vehicle or the
# document, and the rendering service draws it (ADR: A rendering service beside the API); each
# domain's page goes to the service under that site's name. The query goes with
# a 200 rewrite.
#
# Everything else, the bundle, the photographs and /api, goes to the one web app
# that serves both sites (ADR: One web app for every .NET process). Those two
# rules are in netlify.toml, because only a rule written there can add a header
# to what it proxies, and the web app learns which site a request is for from the
# X-Yard-Host header those rules add. Until 19 October they were here, one per
# site, each to a web app of its own.
https://theyard-cosmos.stevenstout.biz/ https://app-theyard-render-ss-zmnetj67bn5h2.azurewebsites.net/site/cosmos 200!
http://theyard-cosmos.stevenstout.biz/* https://theyard-cosmos.stevenstout.biz/:splat 301!
/ https://app-theyard-render-ss-zmnetj67bn5h2.azurewebsites.net/site/sql 200!
